Package: BCAIA
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Covariate-Varying Interaction Analysis for Multivariate Count Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shuangjie", "Zhang", email = "shuangjie.zhang@austin.utexas.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Michael L.", "Patnode", role = "aut"),
    person("Juhee", "Lee", role = "aut"))
Description: Implements the Bayesian covariate-varying factor model of Zhang,
    Patnode and Lee for estimating how the mean abundance and the interaction
    (covariance) structure among features vary with covariates in
    high-dimensional multivariate count data, with a focus on microbiome
    studies. The covariance is modelled through a sparse covariate-dependent
    factor loading matrix with a Dirichlet-Horseshoe prior, and the discrete,
    over-dispersed, zero-inflated counts are handled with a rounded
    multivariate log-normal kernel and mean-constrained Dirichlet process
    mixtures. Posterior inference is carried out by a blocked Gibbs / adaptive
    Metropolis-Hastings sampler implemented in C++.
